<StaticPage
	title="About ShiftBackspace"
	description="Learn about ShiftBackspace, our mission, and the person behind the Microsoft troubleshooting guides and tech reviews you read here."
	icon="💻"
>
	<p>
		ShiftBackspace started with a simple idea: tech help online is scattered, over-complicated, and
		often written by people who've never actually sat down and fixed the problem themselves. We
		wanted one place where you could find clear, practical, no-nonsense answers — the kind you'd get
		from a friend who used to write software for a living, not a content farm chasing keywords.
	</p>
	<p>
		We started with Microsoft products — Windows, Office, OneDrive, Outlook, and the everyday errors
		and settings that send people searching for help — because that's where most people run into
		friction first. From there, we're expanding into broader consumer tech: gadget reviews, smart
		home setup, software tutorials, and home network troubleshooting.
	</p>

	<h2>Who's behind ShiftBackspace</h2>
	<div class="author-card">
		<img src="/dorsey_hollifield.png" alt="Dorsey Hollifield" class="author-photo" />
		<div>
			<p class="author-name">Dorsey Hollifield</p>
			<p class="author-role">Consumer Tech Reviewer &amp; Former Software Engineer, ShiftBackspace</p>
		</div>
	</div>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm <strong>Dorsey Hollifield</strong>, the person writing and editing the guides on
		ShiftBackspace. I spent 8 years as a software engineer at a Seattle-area tech company before
		moving into full-time tech journalism, and I hold a B.S. in Computer Science. That background is
		what shapes how I write: I'd rather explain what's actually happening on your screen than throw
		jargon at you and call it a day.
	</p>
	<p>
		Over the years I've reviewed more than 400 consumer devices and spent countless hours untangling
		Microsoft product quirks — the settings menus that hide the one toggle you need, the error codes
		that mean five different things, the "just restart it" advice that doesn't actually fix anything.
		I've made plenty of my own troubleshooting mistakes along the way, and those experiences are a
		big reason I started ShiftBackspace. I wanted to document the fixes, the shortcuts, and the plain
		explanations I wish someone had given me when I was starting out.
	</p>
	<p>
		Today, I run a dedicated test apartment where I build and tear down smart home systems, and every
		device I review gets at least two weeks of real daily use before I write a word about it. I'm
		still learning too, and I'm comfortable saying when something is outside my experience or when
		you're better off contacting official support directly.
	</p>
	<div class="note-box">
		<span class="note-icon">🛠️</span>
		<span>
			Nothing on this site is official Microsoft support, and it's not a substitute for a
			manufacturer's warranty service or a qualified IT professional for business-critical systems —
			you can read more about that in our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure &amp; Disclaimers</a>
			page. What I can offer is testing, first-hand troubleshooting experience, and an honest attempt
			to cut through the noise.
		</span>
	</div>

	<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
	<ul class="icon-grid">
		<li><span class="emoji">🪟</span><span>Step-by-step fixes for common Windows, Office, and other Microsoft product problems</span></li>
		<li><span class="emoji">🏠</span><span>Smart home setup guides and home network troubleshooting</span></li>
		<li><span class="emoji">📱</span><span>Plain-English software tutorials and how-tos</span></li>
		<li><span class="emoji">🛒</span><span>Honest product and gadget reviews, including some affiliate links (see our <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a>)</span></li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Our editorial approach</h2>
	<p>
		Articles are researched, tested, and periodically reviewed for accuracy as software updates and
		products change. If you ever spot something that looks outdated or wrong, please
		<a href="/contact/">let us know</a> — we'd rather fix it than leave it.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
